---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Terms & Conditions',href:'/terms/'}];
---
<BaseLayout title="Website Terms & Conditions | Talon Expeditions" description="Terms governing use of the Talon Expeditions website. Specific travel bookings are governed by the written proposal, supplier terms, and booking conditions for the trip." breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="content-hero"><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1 class="section-title">Website Terms & Conditions</h1><p class="lead">These terms govern use of the Talon Expeditions website. A specific travel booking may have additional proposal terms, supplier conditions, waivers, payment schedules, cancellation rules, and traveler responsibilities.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow legal-prose"><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 10, 2026</p><div class="legal-note">Website content is general information. The written documents for a specific trip control when they differ from general descriptions on this site.</div>
  <h2>1. Website operator</h2><p>This website is operated by {business.legalName}. References to “Talon Expeditions,” “Talon,” “we,” or “us” on this website refer to that business unless a specific page states otherwise.</p>
  <h2>2. Informational nature of trip content</h2><p>Descriptions of destinations, activities, trip styles, support models, sample schedules, planning examples, and expected inclusions are informational until incorporated into a written proposal or confirmed booking. Availability, price, routes, suppliers, guide assignments, accommodation, transportation, entry requirements, weather, and local conditions can change.</p>
  <h2>3. Travel bookings and supplier terms</h2><p>Many travel services are provided by independent third-party suppliers. Airlines, hotels, cruise lines, tour operators, activity providers, guides, transportation companies, insurers, and other suppliers may impose their own contracts, cancellation policies, waivers, liability limitations, health requirements, or operational rules. Travelers are responsible for reviewing the terms applicable to their booking.</p>
  <h2>4. Activity and travel risk</h2><p>Travel can involve delays, weather, illness, transportation disruption, political conditions, natural hazards, and other uncertainty. Active and skill-based trips can involve additional physical or technical risks. Website descriptions are not medical, safety, or training advice. Travelers are responsible for honestly evaluating their ability, following trip-specific instructions, obtaining appropriate medical advice where needed, and complying with provider requirements.</p>
  <h2>5. Passports, visas, health requirements, and insurance</h2><p>Travelers are responsible for maintaining valid travel documents and satisfying entry, transit, visa, health, vaccination, insurance, and activity requirements applicable to their nationality and itinerary unless a written service explicitly states otherwise. Requirements can change, and government or supplier sources should be checked close to travel.</p>
  <h2>6. Website accuracy</h2><p>We try to keep public information useful and current, but we do not warrant that every page will always reflect the latest supplier, destination, legal, or operational change. Contact us when a decision depends on current availability, price, documentation, or trip-specific conditions.</p>
  <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2><p>Unless otherwise stated, Talon Expeditions owns or licenses the text, branding, page design, and other original website materials presented here. Photography and third-party marks may be owned or licensed by their respective rights holders. Website content may not be republished commercially without permission.</p>
  <h2>8. External links</h2><p>The website may link to suppliers, government resources, travel providers, social platforms, or other third-party sites. Talon Expeditions does not control those sites and is not responsible for their content, availability, security, or privacy practices.</p>
  <h2>9. Limitation of website liability</h2><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Talon Expeditions is not responsible for losses arising solely from reliance on general website information where the current written trip documentation, supplier terms, or official requirements provide different or more specific information. Nothing in these website terms is intended to waive rights that cannot legally be waived.</p>
  <h2>10. Contact</h2><p>Questions about these website terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or mailed to {business.legalName}, {business.address.street}, {business.address.city}, {business.address.region} {business.address.postalCode}, United States.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
